+- **Strengths:** Enables photo-realistic panoramic NeRF reconstruction from a single view by providing geometric initialization [S1].
+- **Limitations:** The trained NeRF is limited to visible regions of the single input panorama; invisible regions are not reconstructed by this method alone [S1].
+- **When to use:** When reconstructing a scene from a single panoramic image and geometric initialization is needed to stabilize the under-constrained optimization [S1].
+- **When not to use:** When full 3D reconstruction including occluded/invisible regions is required without additional inpainting steps [S1].
 
 ## Background
-This method is part of the PERF (Panoramic Neural Radiance Field From a Single Panorama) framework [S1]. It was introduced to address geometry consistency issues in single-view panoramic NeRF reconstruction, where previous methods like SPInNeRF focused on inpainting and perceptual loss without explicit geometry consistency mechanisms [S1]. The approach builds on 360MonoDepth [51] for depth estimation [S1].
+This method was introduced in the PERF (Panoramic Neural Radiance Field From a Single Panorama) paper [S1]. It builds on the observation that existing methods do not fully address geometry consistency in single-view reconstruction [S1]. The approach follows similar principles to 360MonoDepth [S51] for predicting panorama depth by fusing perspective depth maps [S1].
 
